Z||000000||Ferrari_cdn||10-07-2001||07:24 PM||||When I drive her and slow down to a stop, I can feel a faint "clunk" on the shifter.  I accelerate a bit and felt another "clunk".  I played with the fiero, stopping and going, it feels liek something shifted or fell back and forth.  Is this normal or I got something loose, like a fallen nut?<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ferrari_cdn" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_2.JPG"> </A>  <BR>'84 2m4, 4 speed, 106k miles (157k km)  AIM: CanadianFiero||||reg||5
Z||000001||SLYGUY||10-07-2001||09:56 PM||||When I accelerate with WOT and slam the clutch pedal to the floor to shift while dropping the throttle there is a slight clunk too. I think I have either worn engine or worn tranny mounts. If I shift smoothly, it is fine. Do you have a Haynes manual. It is very descriptive as to how to check these mounts. Sounds like they are the culprit.<P>Best of luck!<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ferrari_cdn||10-07-2001||10:05 PM||||WOT?||||reg||5
Z||000003||Old Lar||10-07-2001||10:07 PM||||Could be the dogbone mounts on the engine. Open up the deck lid and see if you can easily move the engine.  Check the dog bone bushings.  The engine will move when the bushings go bad and the clunk you hear is the engine. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||10-08-2001||02:51 AM||||I took a ganders at it when we got together tonight. I'm not sure WHAT to think. Engine mounts seem fine. However, when you grab the fat end of the half-axle, there is a little bit of play on the trans side...<BR>&#0124; &#0124;............../<BR>&#0124; &#0124;[]====[&#0124; &#0124;X===|<BR>&#0124; &#0124;.....^^^^^....\<P>Right there. <BR>If you rotate the tire side, it's solid, but the trans side has a little bit of play. That would explain the ticking sound. I'm thinking worn/defective CV joint right there... Any takers?||216.81.4.183||reg||5
Z||000005||Hippocrat||10-08-2001||03:09 AM||||WOT = Wide Open Throttle<BR>||||reg||1
